== Biography

I studied Electronic Science and Technology at [https://www.zju.edu.cn/english/ Zhejiang University] from September 2021 to June 2025, with a GPA of 91.69 out of 100 (3.98 out of 4.0) and rank 3 out of 91.
My interests include embedded systems, FPGA and reconfigurable computing, optical integrated sensing and communication, and intelligent hardware-software systems.


== Education

- [https://www.zju.edu.cn/english/ Zhejiang University], Electronic Science and Technology, Sep. 2021 -- Jun. 2025
- GPA: 91.69 out of 100 (3.98 out of 4.0), Rank: 3 out of 91


== Research Experience

- *Technology for Treatment Based on Vagus Nerve Stimulation*, Zhejiang Qizhen Medical & Health Technology Co., Ltd., Mar. 2023 -- Jun. 2024
  As a hardware technician, I developed upper-computer software, iterated circuit designs, implemented programs for ESP32 and STM32 microcontrollers, and completed the controller design for high-precision stimulation.
  I also collaborated with Zhejiang University School of Medicine on several small-animal experiments. This work resulted in one patent and one conference poster.

- *Applications in Smart Grid Networking Based on Reconfigurable Devices Like FPGA*, Project Leader, Apr. 2024 -- Aug. 2024
  I worked on functional implementation and performance testing for the AMD Versal ACAP NoC (Network on Chip), exploring high-throughput interconnect structures for IoT-oriented smart-grid networking.


== Project Experience

- *Intelligent Agricultural Robot*, Hardware and Software Design, Feb. 2024 -- May 2024
  I implemented embedded functions on STM32 microcontrollers and integrated information from RGB cameras and ultrasonic sensors for object detection and recognition.
  The project supported functions including Bluetooth control, radar ranging, and infrared obstacle avoidance, and later received awards in related competitions.

- *X-FOCUS: A Desktop Learning Assistant Based on Nano33*, Hardware and Software Design, Sep. 2023 -- Dec. 2023
  I developed deep-learning and image-recognition functions on the Nano33 platform and contributed to Windows-based GUI development using Vue and Python for data interaction and personalized learning reports.


